{"title":"2023 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CoolMathProblems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CoolMathProblems</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(Let&#39;s_first_Understand_the_question)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (Let's first Understand the question)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Magic_Square\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Magic Square</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_harungurcan\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by harungurcan</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreradTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreradTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Harold made a plum pie to take on a picnic. He was able to eat only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the pie, and he left the rest for his friends. A moose came by and ate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of what Harold left behind. After that, a porcupine ate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of what the moose left behind. How much of the original pie still remained after the porcupine left?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/9/e19562d5868a4659821511d7007cda39d3587d92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{12} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{6} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{5}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"389\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Harold ate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cd0f9f9869b39e79527f9010293adf7bfe5210f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the pie. After that, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/f/5ffb79444987a395d27c1dfec4bec1d935460aa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac14=\\frac34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" /> of the pie was left behind.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>The moose ate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da3ee0f0c15573fce7f84645a79d764c0878d37d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac13\\cdot\\frac34 = \\frac14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" /> of the pie. After that, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/064471cc0079dd87dbe3ce880f70bba9f0bfd8a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac34 - \\frac14 = \\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" /> of the pie was left behind.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>The porcupine ate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42fd4d6a4774cf0a8d60c15f92e947927560b3fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac13\\cdot\\frac12 = \\frac16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" /> of the pie. After that, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/9/749ab4237c35a36f63166ad14bfcaf6326712915.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12 - \\frac16 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"134\" height=\"49\" /> of the pie was left behind.</li></ul>\n<p>More simply, we can condense the solution above into the following equation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b79c7d75d940ecb0d045b002bc7f0e20a2bafa3e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(1-\\frac14\\right)\\left(1-\\frac13\\right)\\left(1-\\frac13\\right) = \\frac34\\cdot\\frac23\\cdot\\frac23 = \\frac13.\\]\" width=\"345\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>~apex304, SohumUttamchandani, wuwang2002, TaeKim, Cxrupptedpat, MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because Harold ate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cd0f9f9869b39e79527f9010293adf7bfe5210f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the pie, there must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdcb968f4f3d2e0d78a67fedc92a8d31183b2436.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> of the pie he had at the start left. Because the moose ate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/ebafcc60a28d8759185d7808c60ea53efc73938e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of the pie, there must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/1/611d08a8c57a214b2b964bba16da8157a5b81c9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of the pie the moose had at the start left. Because the porcupine ate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/ebafcc60a28d8759185d7808c60ea53efc73938e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of the pie, there must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/1/611d08a8c57a214b2b964bba16da8157a5b81c9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of the pie the porcupine had at the start left. Therefore, the answer must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/9738b9a2566dee46f74e87541e13e660bf2de678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac34\\times\\frac23\\times\\frac23=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"169\" height=\"49\" /> of the pie left.\n</p><p>~Yuhao2012\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This problem is a great example of the implementation of <b>remaining portions</b>. This concept, in short, refers to the method of finding out what remains of a whole when part of it is taken. If you look closely at our solution, we can see that the denominator is the same when we said Harold ate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cd0f9f9869b39e79527f9010293adf7bfe5210f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the pie and we got <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdcb968f4f3d2e0d78a67fedc92a8d31183b2436.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> of the pie left. We can also see the numerator is just the denominator minus the old denominator.\n</p><p>~Nivaar\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CoolMathProblems\">Video Solution by CoolMathProblems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CoolMathProblems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Pf93RGtKo1I?feature=shared&amp;t=694\">https://youtu.be/Pf93RGtKo1I?feature=shared&amp;t=694</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28A_Clever_Explanation_You.E2.80.99ll_Get_Instantly.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zntZrtsnyxc?si=nM5eWOwNU6HRdleZ&amp;t=557\">https://youtu.be/zntZrtsnyxc?si=nM5eWOwNU6HRdleZ&amp;t=557</a>\n~hsnacademy\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28Let.27s_first_Understand_the_question.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(Let's_first_Understand_the_question)\">Video Solution by Math-X (Let's first Understand the question)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (Let&#39;s first Understand the question)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Ku_c1YHnLt0?si=N3jXnFg5Zy3GCgrB&amp;t=1500\">https://youtu.be/Ku_c1YHnLt0?si=N3jXnFg5Zy3GCgrB&amp;t=1500</a> ~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/WKcH7Cyeipo\">https://youtu.be/WKcH7Cyeipo</a>\n~Education the Study of everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Magic_Square\">Video Solution by Magic Square</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Magic Square\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/-N46BeEKaCQ?t=4814\">https://youtu.be/-N46BeEKaCQ?t=4814</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DBqko2xATxs&amp;t=859\">https://youtu.be/DBqko2xATxs&amp;t=859</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_harungurcan\">Video Solution by harungurcan</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by harungurcan\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oIGy79w1H8o&amp;t=246s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oIGy79w1H8o&amp;t=246s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreradTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreradTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreradTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofoll